-- title:
--   Nonzero continuous H² class matching an unramified carry cocycle
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\zeta$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $q$ be a prime. Write $L = \mathbb{Q}_q\bigl(\{x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q : x^{q^p-1}=1\}\bigr)$ for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q$ generated by the $(q^p-1)$-st roots of unity, and $G_q$ for the group of $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$. The assertion is that the following data exist simultaneously: a unit $u$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ whose underlying element is the image $\iota_q(\zeta)$ of $\zeta$ under the chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra embedding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ obtained by lifting along algebraic closedness; a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $L$ which generates the automorphism group of $L/\mathbb{Q}_q$ (every automorphism lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\varphi$) and is of finite order, and which acts on every $(q^p-1)$-st root of unity in $L$ by $x \mapsto x^{q}$; a unit $\pi$ of $L$ whose underlying element is $q$; normality of $L$ over $\mathbb{Q}_q$; and a function $z : G_q \times G_q \to \mathbb{Z}/p$ lying in `levelCocycles₂` for the restriction homomorphism `primeLocalToGlobal q` from $G_q$ to the automorphism group of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and the representation `ofChar` of the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character `cycloChar p` composed with that homomorphism, i.e. $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with $G_q$ acting through $\chi_p$ (the trivial representation twisted by this character). For these data two conclusions hold. First, the difference of the function $(g_1,g_2) \mapsto u^{\,\mathrm{val}(z(g_1,g_2))}$, written additively in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q^{\times}$ with the exponent the canonical representative in $\{0,\dots,p-1\}$ of $z(g_1,g_2)$, and of `unitsInflate₂` applied to the carry function `carryFun` of $\varphi$ with value $\pi$ in the representation of the automorphism group of $L/\mathbb{Q}_q$ on $L^{\times}$ — the function sending $(g_1,g_2)$ to $\pi$ when the sum of the cyclic logarithms of $g_1$ and $g_2$ to base $\varphi$ reaches $\mathrm{ord}(\varphi)$, and to $1$ otherwise — lies in `levelCoboundaries₂` for [`localGaloisToGlobal q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L41) and the representation of $G_q$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q^{\times}$. Second, the image of $z$ under `continuousH2π`, i.e. its class in the quotient `continuousH2` of `levelCocycles₂` by `levelCoboundaries₂`, is nonzero.
--
--   This is the inhabitedness statement underlying the local invariant at $q$: the cyclic algebra $(L/\mathbb{Q}_q, \varphi, q)$ with $L$ the unramified extension generated by the $(q^p-1)$-st roots of unity has order exactly $p$ in the Brauer group, and its carry cocycle is matched, modulo continuous coboundaries of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q^{\times}$, with $\iota_q(\zeta)^{z}$ for a continuous $2$-cocycle $z$ with values in $\mathbb{Z}/p(\chi_p)$ whose class does not vanish. It is used to construct and characterise the local invariant map, being cited by [`groupCohomology.existsUnique_isLocalInv`](thm.html#groupCohomology.existsUnique_isLocalInv), [`groupCohomology.isLocalInv_localInv_and_bijective`](thm.html#groupCohomology.isLocalInv_localInv_and_bijective) and [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.localInv_eq_of_inflate_eq_kummer`](thm.html#NumberField.PlaceDecomp.localInv_eq_of_inflate_eq_kummer).
